Conclusion
The Cyber Kill Chain framework provides a structured model for understanding how cyberattacks develop from initial reconnaissance to final objectives.
The room demonstrated how attackers move through each phase of an intrusion and how defenders can implement controls to detect and disrupt malicious activity before serious damage occurs.
Understanding the Cyber Kill Chain is essential for SOC analysts, threat hunters, incident responders, and cybersecurity professionals because it helps organizations build proactive and layered defensive strategies against modern threats.
